Description
===========
Honour every atom listed in _NET_WM_STATE, not just the first one.

EWMH defines _NET_WM_STATE as ATOM[]: atoms present in the list MUST be
considered set. updatewindowtype() reads it through getatomprop(), which
returns only element 0, so a client that maps with _NET_WM_STATE_FULLSCREEN
anywhere but the front of the list is never made fullscreen.

Qt hits this whenever a window combines Qt::WindowStaysOnTopHint with
showFullScreen(), since Qt emits ABOVE before FULLSCREEN. flameshot 14 is a
concrete case: its overlay is clamped into the work area below the bar, so
the grabbed image of the bar is drawn just under the real bar and the bottom
of the overlay falls off screen.

hasatomprop() searches the whole list. getatomprop() is left alone and keeps
serving _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE, where taking the front of the list is correct:
that property is an ordered list of preferences, while _NET_WM_STATE is an
unordered set in which every atom counts.

Applies to
==========
dwm git master, commit 44dbc68 (2026-03-13)

